# Model Update Context

This file provides instructions and automation procedures for updating the VS Code `chatLanguageModels.json` configuration file with the latest models from local and networked LM Studio endpoints across **Windows**, **macOS**, and **Linux**.

---

## 1. Target File Paths & Profile Discovery

VS Code stores custom chat model definitions either in the **Default Profile** directory or in a **Custom Profile** directory.

### Path by Operating System

| OS | Default Profile Path | Custom Profile Path |
|----|----------------------|---------------------|
| **Windows** | `%APPDATA%\Code\User\chatLanguageModels.json` | `%APPDATA%\Code\User\profiles\<profile-id>\chatLanguageModels.json` |
| **macOS** | `~/Library/Application Support/Code/User/chatLanguageModels.json` | `~/Library/Application Support/Code/User/profiles/<profile-id>/chatLanguageModels.json` |
| **Linux** | `~/.config/Code/User/chatLanguageModels.json` | `~/.config/Code/User/profiles/<profile-id>/chatLanguageModels.json` |

> [!NOTE]
> If you switch profiles frequently in VS Code, update **both** the active profile (`profiles/<profile-id>/chatLanguageModels.json`) and the base user configuration (`Code/User/chatLanguageModels.json`).

### Active Profile Auto-Detection

To automatically detect the active (most recently modified) profile directory:

**Windows (PowerShell):**
```powershell
# Detect most recently active profile, or fallback to default
$profilesBase = "$env:APPDATA\Code\User\profiles"
$activeProfileDir = Get-ChildItem "$profilesBase\*\globalStorage" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
    Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending | Select-Object -First 1 -ExpandProperty Directory

if ($activeProfileDir) {
    $targetPath = Join-Path $activeProfileDir.FullName "chatLanguageModels.json"
} else {
    $targetPath = "$env:APPDATA\Code\User\chatLanguageModels.json"
}
Write-Host "Target configuration path: $targetPath"
```

**macOS / Linux (Bash):**
```bash
PROFILES_BASE="$HOME/.config/Code/User/profiles"
# On macOS: PROFILES_BASE="$HOME/Library/Application Support/Code/User/profiles"

LATEST_PROFILE=$(ls -td "$PROFILES_BASE"/*/globalStorage 2>/dev/null | head -n 1 | xargs dirname)
if [ -n "$LATEST_PROFILE" ]; then
    TARGET_PATH="$LATEST_PROFILE/chatLanguageModels.json"
else
    TARGET_PATH="$HOME/.config/Code/User/chatLanguageModels.json"
fi
echo "Target configuration path: $TARGET_PATH"
```

---

## 2. Categories and Endpoints

The configuration supports three primary categories, plus the loopback access pattern used by LM Studio:

| Category | Endpoint URL | Description |
|----------|-------------|-------------|
| **Local** | `http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1` | Models hosted on the current machine (loopback) |
| **LM-Link** | `http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1` | All distinct models visible through the local LM Studio endpoint |
| **Remote** | `http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1` | Peer-device models routed through the local endpoint |

> [!NOTE]
> Device names are not fixed across machines. They may be `amd-halo`, `ripper`, `GeForce`, `RyDyn`, or any peer name reported by `lms link status`. Use the runtime output, not a hard-coded list.

---

## 3. Host Context ("Local" vs Peer Devices)

When running on different machines:
- **"Local"** always refers to whichever physical device is executing the script/process (`http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1`).
- To inspect which machine is local vs remote, run:
  ```bash
  lms link status
  ```
  The output lists `This device: <name>` (Local) and the connected peer devices that LM Studio has discovered.
- Peer names are dynamic. They are not guaranteed to be `amd-halo`, `ripper`, or any other static string.
- If you execute this on a peer device, that device becomes `Local` and the workstation or other linked node becomes remote.

---

## 4. URL Conventions

- Use `127.0.0.1` for the local machine loopback address (**not** `localhost`).
- Use hostnames (`amd-halo`, `ripper`) where DNS/mDNS resolution is available on your local network.
- **No remote IPs**: All endpoints resolve locally via hostname or loopback — avoid hardcoded external or link-local IPs (`169.254.x.x`).

---

## 5. Model Discovery & Parsing

### Step 1: Run `lms ls --json`

Use the structured LM Studio output as the source of truth; it exposes `modelKey`, `deviceIdentifier`, and variant metadata without depending on terminal formatting.

```bash
lms ls --json
```

### Step 2: Use the structured fields instead of text parsing

- Each item in the JSON includes a `modelKey` and a `deviceIdentifier`.
- `deviceIdentifier` is `null` for models served by the current machine and a non-null value for peer devices.
- Model variants are represented by the `variants` / `selectedVariant` arrays, so there is no need to parse text like `google/gemma-4-12b-qat (1 variant)`.
- If a model appears on multiple devices, keep a single unique model ID in the final list and classify it by host context.

### Step 3: Categorize Models

- **`Local`**: Models where `deviceIdentifier == null` (or where the device matches the current machine). URL: `http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1`.
- **`Remote`**: Models where `deviceIdentifier != null` and the endpoint is being routed through the local LM Studio loopback. URL: `http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1`.
- **`LM-Link`**: The union of all model IDs visible to the local endpoint. URL: `http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1`.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Do not hard-code peer device names such as `amd-halo` or `ripper` in scripts. The names are runtime-discovered and can vary by machine and cluster topology.

---

## 6. Schema Requirements & Per-Model Context Limits

For each category, define an object with a `models` array in `chatLanguageModels.json`:

```json
{
  "name": "<category-name>",
  "vendor": "customendpoint",
  "apiType": "chat-completions",
  "models": [
    {
      "id": "<model-id>",
      "name": "<display-name>",
      "url": "<endpoint-url>",
      "toolCalling": true,
      "vision": true,
      "maxInputTokens": 65536,
      "maxOutputTokens": 8192
    }
  ]
}
```

### Context Window Allocation (Reasonable Limits $\le$ 100k)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Do not set a blanket 100k context for all models.** Over-allocating context on tiny or embedding models causes out-of-memory errors or exceeds trained context limits. Context sizes must be set to a reasonable limit based on model architecture and parameter count, erroring on the side of higher context by **no more than 100k**:

| Tier | `maxInputTokens` | `maxOutputTokens` | Target Models | Rationale |
|:---|:---:|:---:|:---|:---|
| **94k** | `94208` | `8192` | `google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-qat`<br>`google/gemma-4-31b-qat`<br>`qwen3.8-27b` | Dedicated long-context prose, RFC/architecture documentation, and Mermaid diagramming specialists (optimal 64k–94k). |
| **65k** | `65536` | `8192` | `unsloth/qwen3-coder-next`<br>`qwen/qwen3-coder-next`<br>`qwen3.6-35b-a3b`<br>`qwen3.5-122b-a10b`<br>`gpt-oss-120b`<br>`google/gemma-4-12b-qat`<br>`gemma-4-12b-heretic-abliterated`<br>`qwen/qwen3.5-9b`<br>`nvidia/nemotron-3-super`<br>`nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl`<br>`qwen3-coder-30b-a3b-instruct`<br>`qwen3.6-35b-a3b-uncensored-hauhaucs-aggressive`<br>`qwen3.8-27b-uncensored-hauhaucs-aggressive-mtp` | Primary backend coding agents, deep reasoning MoEs, and mid-size general models. Errs on the high side of their 32k–64k optimal range while avoiding memory bandwidth bottlenecks. |
| **49k** | `49152` | `8192` | `glm-4.7-flash`<br>`qwen/qwen3-4b-2507`<br>`nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-4b`<br>`nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni`<br>`meta/muse-glimmer` | Lightweight 4B models, high-speed UI/frontend specialists, and watchdog/helper models. |
| **32k** | `32768` | `4096` | `qwen3-1.7b` | Tiny 1.7B edge/draft model (native max context is 40,960). |
| **2k** | `2048` | `512` | `text-embedding-nomic-embed-text-v1.5` | Local vector embedding model (native max context is 2,048). |

---

## 7. Safety, Verification & Reload

1. **Backup:** Always create a `.bak` backup copy before writing.
2. **Complete Overwrite:** Write the entire valid JSON structure in one operation. **Never append** to existing arrays to prevent syntax corruption.
3. **Validate Syntax:**
   - PowerShell: `Get-Content $path -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json`
   - Bash: `jq . "$path"`
4. **Verify Endpoints:** Check that no invalid URLs were generated:
   ```powershell
   # Windows PowerShell
   Select-String -Path 'chatLanguageModels.json' -Pattern 'localhost|169\.254\.' | Select-Object LineNumber, Line
   ```
   ```bash
   # macOS / Linux
   grep -n 'localhost\|169\.254\.' chatLanguageModels.json
   ```
   *Expected result: 0 matches.*
5. **Reload VS Code Chat:**
   ```bash
   code --reload-window
   ```
   Or run **Developer: Reload Window** (`Ctrl+Shift+P` / `Cmd+Shift+P`).

---

## 8. Complete Automated PowerShell Script

Save and run this script on Windows to automatically query LM Studio, resolve current and remote model IDs, validate, back up, and update `chatLanguageModels.json` without depending on static hostnames:

```powershell
# update-chat-models.ps1
$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"

# 1. Human-readable name mapping
$nameMap = @{
    "gemma-4-12b-heretic-abliterated" = "Gemma 4 12B Heretic Abliterated"
    "google/gemma-4-12b-qat" = "Gemma 4 12B QAT"
    "google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-qat" = "Gemma 4 26B A4B QAT"
    "google/gemma-4-31b-qat" = "Gemma 4 31B QAT"
    "google/gemma-4-26b-a4b" = "Gemma 4 26B A4B"
    "google/gemma-4-31b" = "Gemma 4 31B"
    "google/gemma-4-12b" = "Gemma 4 12B"
    "google/gemma-4-e4b" = "Gemma 4 E4B"
    "glm-4.7-flash" = "GLM 4.7 Flash"
    "meta/muse-glimmer" = "Meta Muse Glimmer 28B"
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano" = "Nemotron 3 Nano"
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-4b" = "Nemotron 3 Nano 4B"
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni" = "Nemotron 3 Nano Omni 30B-A3B"
    "openai/gpt-oss-20b" = "OpenAI GPT OSS 20B"
    "qwen/qwen2.5-coder-14b" = "Qwen2.5 Coder 14B"
    "qwen/qwen3-4b-2507" = "Qwen 3 4B 2507"
    "qwen/qwen3.5-9b" = "Qwen 3.5 9B"
    "text-embedding-nomic-embed-text-v1.5" = "Text Embedding Nomic Embed Text v1.5"
}

# 2. Per-model context limits (reasonable limits erroring on higher side <= 100k)
$contextMap = @{
    "text-embedding-nomic-embed-text-v1.5" = @{ maxInput = 2048; maxOutput = 512 }
    "qwen/qwen2.5-coder-14b" = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "qwen/qwen3-4b-2507" = @{ maxInput = 49152; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-4b" = @{ maxInput = 49152; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni" = @{ maxInput = 49152; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "meta/muse-glimmer" = @{ maxInput = 49152; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "qwen/qwen3.5-9b" = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "google/gemma-4-12b-qat" = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "gemma-4-12b-heretic-abliterated" = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "openai/gpt-oss-20b" = @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-qat" = @{ maxInput = 94208; maxOutput = 8192 }
    "google/gemma-4-31b-qat" = @{ maxInput = 94208; maxOutput = 8192 }
}

function Build-ModelEntry($id, $url) {
    $displayName = if ($nameMap.ContainsKey($id)) { $nameMap[$id] } else { $id }
    $limits = if ($contextMap.ContainsKey($id)) { $contextMap[$id] } else { @{ maxInput = 65536; maxOutput = 8192 } }
    return [ordered]@{
        id              = $id
        name            = $displayName
        url             = $url
        toolCalling     = $true
        vision          = $true
        maxInputTokens  = $limits.maxInput
        maxOutputTokens = $limits.maxOutput
    }
}

# 3. Use the authoritative LM Studio JSON output instead of fixed hostnames
Write-Host "Fetching authoritative model list from 'lms ls --json'..." -ForegroundColor Cyan
$lmsModels = @((lms ls --json) | ConvertFrom-Json)

$localIds = @()
$remoteIds = @()
foreach ($model in $lmsModels) {
    $id = $model.modelKey
    if ($null -eq $model.deviceIdentifier) {
        $localIds += $id
    }
    else {
        $remoteIds += $id
    }
}

$localIds = $localIds | Sort-Object -Unique
$remoteIds = $remoteIds | Sort-Object -Unique

# 4. LM-Link includes every model currently visible through the local loopback
$apiModels = @()
try {
    $apiModels = @((Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1/models").data | Select-Object -ExpandProperty id)
}
catch {
    $apiModels = @()
}
$lmLinkIds = @($apiModels + $localIds + $remoteIds | Sort-Object -Unique)

# 5. Construct category objects
$categories = @(
    [ordered]@{
        name    = "Local"
        vendor  = "customendpoint"
        apiType = "chat-completions"
        models  = @($localIds | ForEach-Object { Build-ModelEntry $_ "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1" })
    },
    [ordered]@{
        name    = "LM-Link"
        vendor  = "customendpoint"
        apiType = "chat-completions"
        models  = @($lmLinkIds | ForEach-Object { Build-ModelEntry $_ "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1" })
    },
    [ordered]@{
        name    = "Remote"
        vendor  = "customendpoint"
        apiType = "chat-completions"
        models  = @($remoteIds | ForEach-Object { Build-ModelEntry $_ "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1" })
    }
)

$jsonContent = $categories | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 5

# 6. Resolve target paths (active profile + base User configuration)
$targets = @()
$baseConfig = "$env:APPDATA\Code\User\chatLanguageModels.json"
$targets += $baseConfig

$activeProfileDir = Get-ChildItem "$env:APPDATA\Code\User\profiles\*\globalStorage" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
    Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending | Select-Object -First 1 -ExpandProperty Directory

if ($activeProfileDir) {
    $targets += (Join-Path $activeProfileDir.FullName "chatLanguageModels.json")
}

$targets = $targets | Select-Object -Unique

# 7. Validate & Write
foreach ($target in $targets) {
    if (Test-Path $target) {
        Copy-Item -Path $target -Destination "$target.bak" -Force
        Write-Host "Created backup: $target.bak"
    }
    [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($target, $jsonContent, [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8)
    Write-Host "Successfully updated: $target" -ForegroundColor Green

    $null = Get-Content $target -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
}

# 8. Verify no invalid URLs were generated
$invalidMatches = Select-String -Path $targets -Pattern 'localhost|169\.254\.'
if ($invalidMatches.Count -gt 0) {
    Write-Warning "Found invalid URLs in output!"
    $invalidMatches | Format-Table LineNumber, Line
} else {
    Write-Host "URL verification passed (0 invalid URLs)." -ForegroundColor Green
}

Write-Host "To apply changes in VS Code, run: code --reload-window" -ForegroundColor Cyan
```
